{
 "about": "Gag schools (Sam, 11 Nov 2026: 'if I ask you to use south park gags then you should only utilize south park gags'). Every picture gag in the kit belongs to one or more schools: a style family learnt from a study. A scene plan picks its schools with \"gags\": [\"southpark\"]; gag_lint.py then refuses any gag card or gag camera move that no chosen school owns. 'house' is the neutral grammar (chapter titles, the spoken-number card, lower text, true-scale bars, gentle Ken Burns moves) and is always allowed. A card matches a recipe when every key in the recipe's 'match' equals the card's value (\"*\" = any value present). Status 'built' = in the kit today; 'to build' = studied, not yet a kit kind.",
